# Share URI ↔ local map (Cursor)

**Invariant:** `map(ShareURI → local mount) = awareness for batch/script host work` · `¬ substitute for MCP on Share URIs` · durable prose cites Share URIs only.

On Cursor IDE and cursor-sdk hosts that mount the ULG shares, agents know these equivalences so they can author scripts, batch jobs, and host-side loops against the mounts. Mounts may change; **durable prose cites Share URIs only**.

| Share | Local mount (Cursor / cursor_sdk) |
|---|---|
| `cortex://` | `/mnt/torus/mcp-data/files/` |
| `workspaces://` | `/mnt/torus/projects/` |

Examples: `cortex://notes/system/specs/foo.md` → `/mnt/torus/mcp-data/files/notes/system/specs/foo.md` · `workspaces://universal-llm-gateway/libs/x.py` → `/mnt/torus/projects/universal-llm-gateway/libs/x.py`.

## MCP stays normal (do not replace)

**Default for document work:** call MCP on the Share URI (`fs` / `fs_read` / `md_list` / section-scoped `md_read`, `cortex`, …). Those tools supply metadata, lease/CAS, section scoping, and context-window protection that a raw mount read does not.

| Use | Path |
|---|---|
| Navigate / read / edit Markdown and Share-backed docs | MCP on `cortex://…` / `workspaces://…` (normal) |
| Batch scripts, host loops, one-shot lookup when MCP is the wrong tool | Local mount under the table above (awareness only) |

`¬` drop MCP for `Read`/`Grep`/shell on the mount just because the map exists. Local section APIs (`libs/markdown_sections`) are for in-process/script use of the same mounts — not a seat substitute for MCP `md_*`.

## Access policy

**Mapped mounts = host read/lookup affordance, not a write grant.** A visible path under these roots does not authorize durable mutation.

| Class | Where |
|---|---|
| **Doc / Share I/O (default)** | MCP tools with Share URIs |
| **Batch / script host reads** | Share URI mounts when the work is offline batch or scripted against the filesystem |
| **Writes** and write-bearing repo shell (`pytest`, `ruff` on tracked tree, `git` that mutates state) | **Verified assigned worktree only** — path `{GIT_INTEGRATION_WORKTREE_ROOT}/{repo_basename}/lane-{thread_id}` (repo name appears exactly once; branch `cursor-sdk/lane-{thread_id}`). SoT: `runbook:grok-host-preflight` (`cortex://notes/system/runbooks/grok-host-preflight.md`) § Assigned worktree resolution · § Checkout isolation |
| **Raw IDE/shell writes** without verified lane-B assignment (including hub / lane-A shared checkout under `workspaces://universal-llm-gateway/…`) | **Refuse** — commission **Composer** via `team_dispatch` `seat=cursor-sdk` `lane=B`; do not write on hub |

**Durable Markdown edits** (cortex or workspaces): managed `fs` `md_*` with lease/CAS (`expected_sha256` where required), or a CLI that invokes the same managed op — not unverified shell `Write` against Share mount roots.

## Citation

Reports, closeouts, assertions, packets, and handoffs reference `cortex://…` / `workspaces://…` — ¬ bake `/mnt/torus/…` into durable text. Local paths are a batch/script affordance, not the public address.

Companion (Grok Bot / host shell): `runbook:grok-bot-boot` · `a:44683`. Checkout/write isolation for host grants: `runbook:grok-host-preflight` · `cortex://notes/system/runbooks/grok-host-preflight.md`.
